{"id":"91019f84-54a8-4996-9da9-fc01b2e7debf","object":"chat.completion","created":1791595842,"model":"deepseek-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","reasoning_content":"Now I know the zttp:sql API:

- `sql(name, statement)` registers a statement at module scope (effect write, returns boolean).
- `sqlMany(name, params?)` returns `object[]` (effect read).

So:

```ts
import { sql, sqlMany } from "zttp:sql";

structural Guard<T> = Proof<T, "state_isolated" | "result_safe" | "optional_safe" | "canonical">;

sql("listUsers", "SELECT id, name FROM users");

export function handler(req: Request): Guard<Response> {
  const users = sqlMany("listUsers");
  return Response.json({ users: users });
}
```

